<title>USA: Home Federal sees saving on premiums.</title>
<headline>Home Federal sees saving on premiums.</headline>
<dateline>SEYMOUR, Ind. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Home Federal Bancorp said Monday it expects to see its annual FDIC Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF) expense reduced to $313,000 from $1.1 million. It said this amounts to about $0.22 per share in after-tax savings annually.</p>
<p>Since the new rates do not go into effect until January 1, 1997, it said the company will realize an $0.11 per share savings in the current fiscal year.</p>
<p>Earlier, Home Federal said it recorded a $3 million special SAIF assessment in its September 30 first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
